## HOW YOU ARE SCORED
The operator is benchmarked by the contest harness against a shipped baseline
implementation, on 7 public performance shapes, using device-event timing with
>=500 ms of conditioning per measurement and per-variant medians. The score is
`G_ref_public`: the weight-normalised geometric mean of `baseline_ms / your_ms`
across those shapes. `G = 1.0` means "no faster than the baseline". Lower
absolute latency on the shapes that carry weight is the only thing that helps.

A candidate is only kept if **all** of these hold, in this order:
1. `scripts/build.sh` compiles the Ascend C kernel (BiSheng/`ccec`, 910B3).
2. The official correctness + robustness suite passes (60 public cases: shape
   edge cases, FP16 subnormal/underflow cases, adversarial alignment and
   cancellation fixtures seeded from a strict precision contract).
3. The public benchmark completes.
Anything else scores zero for that candidate, so **numerical safety and
compilability are worth more than theoretical speed**.

